xt-laipath is a Rust port of the lai-path implementation supplied for this project.
Numerical integration, root-finding, and error-handling algorithms are derived
from the GNU Scientific Library (GSL). Reviewed upstream version: GSL 2.8.
Upstream source: https://ftp.gnu.org/gnu/gsl/gsl-2.8.tar.gz

Complete upstream copyright notices are retained in GSL-COPYRIGHTS.txt.
This crate is licensed under GNU GPL version 3 or, at your option, any later
version. The complete license text is provided in COPYING.

Porting changes include corrections to error estimates, integration ordering
and return branches, Brent swap conditions, root-solver state management,
histogram boundaries, and LAI error propagation. Optional Python bindings
are maintained separately from the default Rust interface.
